    [BugFix][EPLB] Warn and ignore unsupported MRv2 EPLB configuration fields (#19395)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Model Runner V2 currently rejects any unsupported
    `additional_config.eplb_config` field with an exception. This change
    makes it warn and filter unsupported top-level EPLB and `stair_config`
    fields, while preserving supported configuration values. Legacy MRv1
    environment controls are also warned and ignored under MRv2.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes: MRv2 no longer fails on unsupported EPLB additional-config fields;
    unsupported values are ignored with a warning.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Updated `tests/ut/test_platform.py` for warning/filtering behavior.
    - Ran Python syntax checks.
    - Ran `git diff --check`.
    - CI will run the unit tests and pre-commit checks.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    Signed-off-by: x00946744 <xingbowen1@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: x00946744 <xingbowen1@huawei.com>

